# Public wrapper pairs deliberately share their implementation files because
# each session wrapper exists solely to render its corresponding primary view.
multiple-public-types | src/domain/redacted.rs | The session view is the primary view's shared-budget formatting adapter.
multiple-public-types | src/domain/redacted_keyed_map.rs | The session view is the primary keyed-map view's shared-budget formatting adapter.
multiple-public-types | src/domain/redacted_keyed_value.rs | The session view is the primary keyed-value view's shared-budget formatting adapter.
multiple-public-types | src/domain/redacted_map.rs | The session view is the primary map view's shared-budget formatting adapter.
multiple-public-types | src/json/redacted_json.rs | The session view is the primary JSON view's shared-budget formatting adapter.
multiple-public-types | src/json/redacted_json_text.rs | The session view is the primary JSON-text view's shared-budget formatting adapter.
multiple-public-types | src/policy/redaction_policy_builder.rs | Builder views are inseparable mutable projections of the root builder.
multiple-public-types | src/policy/redaction_session.rs | Session budget types form one shared accounting model.
multiple-public-types | src/attribute.rs | Attribute variants and their key value objects form one static metadata vocabulary.
multiple-public-types | src/constraint.rs | Constraint values and their supporting enums form one cohesive constraint vocabulary.
multiple-public-types | src/query.rs | Attribute queries and path-resolution errors form one query contract.
multiple-public-types | src/relation.rs | Static field paths and relation value objects form one relation contract.
multiple-public-types | src/type_metadata.rs | Named type metadata and structural descriptors form one recursive metadata contract.
multiple-public-types | src/type_shape.rs | Type shapes, capabilities, and references form one recursive type system contract.
